  "content": {
    "id": "p34-q04-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Find the coefficient of $x^5$ in $\\left(x^2-\\dfrac{1}{x^3}\\right)^{10}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-120$\n\nThe general term has power $x^{20-5k}$; set $20-5k=5$, giving $k=3$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\nT_k&=\\binom{10}{k}(x^2)^{10-k}\\left(-\\frac{1}{x^3}\\right)^k\\\\\nT_k&=\\binom{10}{k}(-1)^k x^{20-5k}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nFor the $x^5$ term,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n20-5k&=5\\\\\nk&=3.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe coefficient is\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\binom{10}{3}(-1)^3&=-\\binom{10}{3}\\\\\n\\binom{10}{3}(-1)^3&=-120.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 68
  },
